WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:05.600
For the second night running, Grenfell Tower burned.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.920
Pockets of fire remained in difficult-to-reach places.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.500
Fire crews have searched almost all the building.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:18.170
But the toll of this blaze is still far from
clear.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.300
Residents of the tower block spent the night in makeshift shelters.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.789
The ordeal they have been through is difficult to imagine.

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:33.050
And that ordeal continues -- as they wait
for news of loved ones, friends, neighbours.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.499
So many are missing.

00:00:34.499 --> 00:00:38.399
And so many must be feared dead.

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:41.940
Amid the grief and horror, 
the question why.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:47.639
How could this building, renovated only last year, be engulfed so quickly?

00:00:47.639 --> 00:00:50.210
How could safety measures apparently fail?

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:52.690
"The fire was quite small to start off with.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:57.038
There was a gentleman standing in the crowd stating that that

00:00:57.038 --> 00:00:58.749
was his flat that was on

00:00:58.749 --> 00:01:01.499
fire, and a refrigerator had blown up.

00:01:01.499 --> 00:01:03.589
Like I said, very small fire.

00:01:03.589 --> 00:01:08.070
And within minutes, from the left and right
and above, it just spread so rapidly."

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:11.420
"It's the cladding, it's the cladding.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.430
I spoke to a resident who had been living
there for 40 years and she said that there

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:16.930
has been fires there but they've always been contained.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:22.690
This is the first fire that has spread around the building and spread so fast and that cladding

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:25.590
went up less than a year ago."

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:29.260
"But the problem is, there are no fire alarms running, working.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:30.260
I don't know why."

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:31.260
"I haven't heard no alarm.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.320
I've only heard in my house smoke alarm."

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.750
An activist group says it had been predicting
a catastrophe for years.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:44.120
This is one image from the group's website.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:51.090
"We repeatedly reported concerns to the tenant management organisation for Kensington and

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:56.200
Chelsea including the fire safety concerns
which were not investigated during the regeneration

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.190
works."

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:02.229
The authorities are promising a full investigation.

00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:07.840
It's still far too early to really know what
happened.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.099
Amid the trauma -- signs of solidarity.

00:02:11.099 --> 00:02:18.639
Food, clothes, toys -- donations have been
pouring in, for those who lost their homes

00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:21.260
and everything in them.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:26.930
"The response is unbelievable, I mean the
church was filled with donations almost by

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:27.930
ten o'clock."

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:33.030
“We love our community, we love our community
and we are heartbroken for our community.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:36.189
This is terrible, this is a disaster for this
community.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:43.170
But, we are pulling together; the people that
have nothing are here getting things for the

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:45.290
people who have nothing.”

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:49.469
A community hit by tragedy.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:55.340
The true extent of that tragedy will only
become clear in the days ahead -- as rescuers

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.860
comb the shell of Grenfell Tower.

